save_compchem.geometry_optimisation_cell

    _definition.id                '_compchem.geometry_optimisation_cell'
    _alias.definition_id          '_compchem_geometry_optimisation_cell'
    _definition.update            2026-04-24
    _description.text
    ;
    It can be "fixed" for no cell optimisation, "isotropic" or "anisotropic" for cell relaxation calculations.
    ;
    _name.category_id             '_compchem'
    _name.object_id               'geometry_optimisation_cell'
    _type.purpose                 State
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Text
    loop_                      
        _enumeration_set.state 
        _enumeration_set.detail
        'fixed'                                  ' no cell optimisation'
        'isotropic'                              ' Isotropic cell relaxation.'
        'anisotropic'                            ' Anisotropic cell relaxation'

save_

save_compchem.geometry_optimisation_atoms

    _definition.id                '_compchem.geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _alias.definition_id          '_compchem_geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _definition.update            2026-04-24
    _description.text
    ;
    It can be "fixed", "all", "intermolecular only", "hydrogens" or "non hydrogens"

    Examples:
    "all"
    ;
    _name.category_id             '_compchem'
    _name.object_id               'geometry_optimisation_atoms'
    _type.purpose                 State
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Text
    loop_                      
        _enumeration_set.state 
        _enumeration_set.detail
        'fixed'                                  ' no atoms position optimisation (only cell dimesions are optimised)'
        'all'                                    ' an all atoms geometry optimization.'
        'intermolecular only'                    ' molecules are kept rigid and only optimise their position and orientation.'
        'hydrogens'                              ' optimisation of only H atoms'
        'non hydrogens'                          ' non H atoms are optimised while H atoms are kept at fixed positions/orientation from the bonded atom.'

save_

