save_forcefield.parameterization_description

    _definition.id                '_forcefield.parameterization_description'
    _alias.definition_id          '_forcefield_parameterization_description'
    _definition.update            2026-04-24
    _description.text
    ;
    Briefly describes the primary method used to derive the intramolecular, electrostatic, dispersion/repulsion force field parameters.

    Examples:
    "Fitting to gas-phase QM data", "Transferable parameters based on atom types"
    ;
    _name.category_id             '_forcefield'
    _name.object_id               'parameterization_description'
    _type.purpose                 Describe
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Text

save_

save_forcefield.parameterization_method

    _definition.id                '_forcefield.parameterization_method'
    _alias.definition_id          '_forcefield_parameterization_method'
    _definition.update            2026-04-24
    _description.text
    ;
    The parametrisation method used (for example the exchange-correlation functional and basis set used in the gas-phase quantum mechanical calculations when fitting force field parameters) or database from which parameters are taken if no calculation is performed. As a rule of thumb, quantum mechanical methods should be described as <Functional>-<dispersion correction>/<basis set> (e.g. PBE-D3/cc-pvtz).

    Examples:
    - "MP2/6-31G(d,p)"
    - "B3LYP/aug-cc-pVTZ"
    - ...
    ;
    _name.category_id             '_forcefield'
    _name.object_id               'parameterization_method'
    _type.purpose                 Describe
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Text

save_

